        "after": [
          "e02"
        ],
        "gap": "P14D"
      },
      "kind": "speech",
      "place": "nursery",
      "text": "John was away all day and some nights on serious cases; he refused to repaper the room, saying she was letting it get the better of her, and called her a blessed little goose; she said it was silly to make him uncomfortable for a whim.",
      "who": [
        {
          "id": "john",
          "role": "speaker"
        },
        {
          "id": "narrator",
          "role": "addressee"
        }
      ],
      "src": [
        "P41",
        "P42",
        "P51",
        "P52",
        "P53",
        "P54",
        "P55",
        "P56",
        "P57",
        "P58"
      ],
      "says": "You know the place is doing you good, and really, dear, I don't care to renovate the house just for a three months' rental."
    },
    {
