    {
      "id": "e23",
      "when": {
        "seq": 23
      },
      "kind": "act",
      "place": "nursery",
      "text": "She brought out a rope that Jennie never found, in case the woman should get out, tried in vain to move the bed, bit a corner of it, peeled all the paper she could reach, and began to creep around the room in the rubbed streak, feeling that she was one of the women who come out of the paper.",
